{"page":"RPTOR","gene":"RPTOR","accession":"Q8N122","protein":"Regulatory-associated protein of mTOR","length":1335,"events":["Alternative splicing"],"canonical":{"accession":"Q8N122-1","name":"1","synonyms":[],"notes":[],"transcripts":{"ensembl":["ENST00000306801.8"],"refseq":["NM_020761.3"],"refseqProteins":["NP_065812.1"],"maneSelect":true,"decay":[],"onlyDecay":false},"model":{"entry":"AF-Q8N122-F1","cif":"https://alphafold.ebi.ac.uk/files/AF-Q8N122-F1-model_v6.cif","meanPlddt":79.8,"plddt":[[0,20],[50,1],[70,4],[90,10],[70,5],[50,8],[70,2],[50,3],[70,3],[90,11],[70,15],[90,8],[70,1],[90,20],[70,2],[90,1],[70,1],[90,27],[70,1],[90,25],[70,5],[90,36],[70,14],[50,1],[70,1],[50,10],[70,4],[90,14],[70,4],[90,20],[70,4],[50,8],[70,14],[90,1],[70,2],[90,23],[70,2],[90,2],[70,2],[90,3],[70,1],[90,1],[70,1],[90,45],[70,19],[90,14],[70,3],[50,5],[70,4],[90,9],[70,4],[90,14],[70,4],[90,2],[70,2],[90,2],[70,1],[90,12],[70,3],[90,40],[70,1],[90,101],[70,3],[50,1],[70,8],[90,34],[70,1],[90,2],[70,1],[90,3],[70,9],[50,4],[0,84],[50,2],[70,2],[50,9],[0,15],[50,1],[70,2],[90,30],[70,6],[50,4],[0,105],[50,2],[70,4],[90,6],[70,1],[90,2],[70,6],[50,2],[70,1],[50,1],[70,8],[90,23],[70,1],[90,1],[70,1],[90,31],[70,2],[90,20],[70,4],[90,32],[70,4],[90,11],[70,4],[50,4],[70,2],[90,38],[70,3],[90,8],[70,5],[90,16],[70,1],[90,2],[70,2],[90,19],[70,6],[90,15],[70,2],[90,10],[70,3],[90,1],[70,1],[90,5],[70,2],[90,8],[70,1],[90,8],[70,3],[90,8],[70,3],[50,1],[70,3],[90,31],[70,2],[50,2],[0,1]]}},"features":[{"type":"Modified residue","start":44,"end":44,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":122,"end":122,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":696,"end":696,"description":"Phosphoserine; by MAPK8"},{"type":"Glycosylation","start":700,"end":700,"description":"O-linked (GlcNAc) threonine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":706,"end":706,"description":"Phosphothreonine; by MAPK8"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":719,"end":719,"description":"Phosphoserine; by RPS6KA1"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":721,"end":721,"description":"Phosphoserine; by RPS6KA1"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":722,"end":722,"description":"Phosphoserine; by AMPK and RPS6KA1"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":738,"end":738,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":791,"end":791,"description":"Phosphoserine; by PKA"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":792,"end":792,"description":"Phosphoserine; by AMPK"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":836,"end":836,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":855,"end":855,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":859,"end":859,"description":"Phosphoserine; by MTOR"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":863,"end":863,"description":"Phosphoserine; by MAPK8, MTOR and NLK"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":865,"end":865,"description":"Phosphothreonine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":877,"end":877,"description":"Phosphoserine; by TBK1"},{"type":"Cross-link","start":932,"end":932,"description":"Glycyl lysine isopeptide (Lys-Gly) (interchain with G-Cter in ubiquitin)"},{"type":"Cross-link","start":948,"end":948,"description":"Glycyl lysine isopeptide (Lys-Gly) (interchain with G-Cter in ubiquitin)"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":982,"end":982,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Repeat","start":1020,"end":1061,"description":"WD 1"},{"type":"Repeat","start":1065,"end":1106,"description":"WD 2"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":1097,"end":1097,"description":"N6-acetyllysine"},{"type":"Repeat","start":1121,"end":1160,"description":"WD 3"},{"type":"Repeat","start":1164,"end":1203,"description":"WD 4"},{"type":"Repeat","start":1209,"end":1249,"description":"WD 5"},{"type":"Repeat","start":1251,"end":1291,"description":"WD 6"},{"type":"Repeat","start":1299,"end":1335,"description":"WD 7"}],"interfaces":{},"subunit":[{"topic":"Subunit","text":"Part of the mechanistic target of rapamycin complex 1 (mTORC1) which contains MTOR, MLST8 and RPTOR (PubMed:12408816, PubMed:24403073, PubMed:25940091, PubMed:27909983, PubMed:29236692, PubMed:31601708, PubMed:31601764, PubMed:36697823). mTORC1 associates with AKT1S1/PRAS40, which inhibits its activity (PubMed:17386266, PubMed:31601764). mTORC1 associates with DEPTOR, which regulates its activity (PubMed:34519268, PubMed:34519269). mTORC1 binds to and is inhibited by FKBP12-rapamycin (PubMed:12408816, PubMed:15066126). Forms a complex with MTOR under both leucine-rich and -poor conditions (PubMed:12408816, PubMed:25940091, PubMed:31601708, PubMed:31601764). Interacts with (via TOS motifs) EIF4EBP1 and RPS6KB1; interaction is independent of its association with MTOR (PubMed:12150925, PubMed:12150926, PubMed:12747827, PubMed:24403073). Binds preferentially to poorly or non-phosphorylated forms of EIF4EBP1, and this binding is critical to the ability of MTOR to catalyze phosphorylation (PubMed:12747827, PubMed:24403073). Interacts with ULK1 in a nutrient-dependent manner; the interaction is reduced during starvation (PubMed:19211835). Interacts with GTP-bound form of RagA/RRAGA or RagB/RRAGB and GDP-bound form of RagC/RRAGC or RagD/RRAGD, promoting recruitment of mTORC1 to the lysosomes (PubMed:31601708, PubMed:31601764). Interacts (when phosphorylated by AMPK) with 14-3-3 protein, leading to inhibition of its activity (PubMed:18439900). Interacts with SPAG5; SPAG5 competes with MTOR for RPTOR-binding, resulting in decreased mTORC1 formation (PubMed:23953116). Interacts with WAC; WAC positively regulates MTOR activity by promoting the assembly of the TTT complex composed of TELO2, TTI1 and TTI2 and the RUVBL complex composed of RUVBL1 and RUVBL2 into the TTT-RUVBL complex which leads to the dimerization of the mTORC1 complex and its subsequent activation (PubMed:26812014). Interacts with G3BP1 (PubMed:23953116). The complex formed with G3BP1 and SPAG5 is increased by oxidative stress (PubMed:23953116). Interacts with HTR6 (PubMed:23027611). Interacts with PIH1D1 (PubMed:24036451). Interacts with LARP1 (PubMed:25940091). Interacts with BRAT1 (PubMed:25657994). Interacts with SIK3 (PubMed:30232230). Interacts with SLC38A7; this interaction mediates the recruitment of mTORC1 to the lysosome and its subsequent activation (PubMed:35561222). Interacts with ARF5 (PubMed:36735494)"},{"topic":"Subunit","text":"(Microbial infection) Interacts with vaccinia virus protein F17; this interaction dysregulates mTOR"}],"isoforms":[{"accession":"Q8N122-2","name":"2","synonyms":[],"notes":[],"length":379,"transcripts":{"ensembl":["ENST00000570891.5"],"refseq":[],"refseqProteins":[],"maneSelect":false,"decay":[],"onlyDecay":false},"segments":[[1,1,379]],"edits":[{"start":380,"end":1335,"original":"QAWDLAVDICLSQLPTIIEEGTAFRHSPFFAEQLTAFQVW","replacement":"","added":0}],"missing":956,"replaced":0,"novel":0,"foldedAbsent":713,"foldedMissing":713,"features":[[2,1,0],[3,1,0],[4,1,0],[5,1,0],[6,1,0],[7,1,0],[8,1,0],[9,1,0],[10,1,0],[11,1,0],[12,1,0],[13,1,0],[14,1,0],[15,1,0],[16,1,0],[17,1,0],[18,1,0],[19,1,0],[20,42,0],[21,42,0],[22,1,0],[23,40,0],[24,40,0],[25,41,0],[26,41,0],[27,37,0]],"interfaces":{},"model":{"entry":"AF-Q8N122-2-F1","cif":"https://alphafold.ebi.ac.uk/files/AF-Q8N122-2-F1-model_v6.cif","meanPlddt":89.7,"plddt":[[0,12],[50,8],[70,22],[50,10],[70,2],[90,19],[70,7],[90,132],[70,16],[50,6],[70,5],[90,39],[70,18],[90,83]],"losingConfidence":0}},{"accession":"Q8N122-3","name":"3","synonyms":["RAPTOR_v2"],"notes":[],"length":1177,"transcripts":{"ensembl":["ENST00000544334.6"],"refseq":["NM_001163034.2"],"refseqProteins":["NP_001156506.1"],"maneSelect":false,"decay":[],"onlyDecay":false},"segments":[[1,1,503],[504,662,674]],"edits":[{"start":504,"end":661,"original":"SCQADLVKDNGHKYFLSVLADPYMPAEHRTMTAFILAVIV","replacement":"","added":0}],"missing":158,"replaced":0,"novel":0,"foldedAbsent":157,"foldedMissing":157,"features":[],"interfaces":{},"model":{"entry":"AF-Q8N122-3-F1","cif":"https://alphafold.ebi.ac.u